# Normalise every text file to LF in the repository and on checkout.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Git for Windows default) checks these
# files out with CRLF while the committed blobs stay LF. Biome's default
# `lineEnding` is `lf`, so `biome format` then reports ~96 files as unformatted
# on Windows even though nothing has actually drifted — and any `--write` looks
# like it is about to produce a huge diff that git would silently discard.
#
# `text=auto` still lets Git detect and leave binaries alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
